+## Kenney Furniture Kit 2.0 - private rooms
+
+Kenney's [Furniture Kit](https://kenney.nl/assets/furniture-kit) supplies
+unmodified CC0 1.0 GLB files for the private-room furniture renderer. See the
+[original archive notice](src/assets/kenney-furniture/LICENSE.txt). The official
+ZIP SHA-256 is
+`e67652d0932cee41683f74711c03d3e192a2af9979ef8e6b237711f5482d46b0`.
+
+| Saved furniture kind | Original file in `Models/GLTF format/` |
+| --- | --- |
+| Table | `tableRound.glb` |
+| Chair | `chairCushion.glb` |
+| Open shelf | `bookcaseOpen.glb` |
+| Shelf contents | `books.glb`, `cardboardBoxClosed.glb`, `plantSmall2.glb`, `radio.glb` |
+| Plant | `pottedPlant.glb` |
+
+The models are bundled at build time and loaded from the game origin. The
+client fits the models to the saved floor anchor and the existing collision
+footprint. The open shelves also reuse the original stoneware jar profile.
+The room retains the existing item IDs, layout and editing rules.
+The catalogue geometry remains available if a model fails to load and is
+still used for outdoor and public placements. Private rooms have no bed or
+lamp in the existing save catalogue.
+
+[Quaternius Furniture Pack](https://quaternius.com/packs/furniture.html) (CC0)
+was considered. Kenney offers matching GLBs for all four saved furniture
+kinds and needs no format conversion.
+
+## Street and house exterior
+
+The village exterior reuses the original local cottage and lantern alongside fitted roof, timber, bench and sign meshes from the Kenney Fantasy Town Kit 2.0 (CC0). [Sources, author notice and reproducible extraction](src/assets/town-exterior/README.md).
+
 ## R8 local workshop additions
@@ -152 +184,20 @@ No terrain demo server patch or additional downloaded art was used.
 The optional background music is an original procedural bell/pad miniature implemented for Little Worlds in `src/client/ambient-music.ts`. Web Audio oscillators synthesize its notes locally; there are no sampled recordings, downloaded tracks, external audio services or new asset licences. Messenger is an atmosphere reference only; its music was not copied.
+
+## Bothouse residents on visited planets
+
+The visitor sees articulated meshes in Little Worlds' village materials.
+The six modelled looks use Bothouse's public character designs as references.
+The buildings, landing pad and ground movement come from Little Worlds.
+For each character's references and modelled details, see the
+[resident model notes](docs/integration/bothouse-resident-models.md).
+
+Bothouse's [desk frame reference](https://github.com/zuiho-kai/bothouse/blob/8ec73a8f32573b5307922df3c79675a934cdefb7/dsh/collab/desk/index.html)
+and [avatar credits](https://github.com/zuiho-kai/bothouse/blob/8ec73a8f32573b5307922df3c79675a934cdefb7/dsh/collab/avatars/README.md)
+identify the artwork and its upstream authors. Copyright 2026 zuiho-kai and
+Bothouse contributors. Bothouse's Apache-2.0 code licence preserves the terms
+of third-party artwork. Check the applicable design rights for your deployment.
+
+A resident with a custom appearance uses the village's generic body. An avatar
+cleared for visitor display can appear on its badge and in the resident list.
+The list credits the pack, author and licence supplied by its publisher. The
+scene needs no sprite-sheet installation or desktop-pet animation files.
